The data files below contain values retrieved from public scientific databases.
They are redistributed for reproducibility of the pre-registered studies. Each
source retains its own licence, which governs that data independently of the
Apache-2.0 licence covering this project's code.

ChEMBL  --  CC BY-SA 3.0
    Files: data/corpus_ACHE.json, data/study_ache_affinity.json,
           data/study_affinity_corrected.json, data/study_inputs/ache_bench.json,
           runs/*/input.yaml for the 17 runs whose manifest `job` is a CHEMBL accession
           (kind "ache-affinity") -- these carry the ligand SMILES the benchmark folded
    (This list is enumerated by filename and is verified against the repository by
     platform/tests/test_platform.py: any tracked file containing ChEMBL identifiers
     must appear here, because a file omitted from the carve-out would otherwise be
     offered downstream under Apache-2.0 -- a sublicensing grant this project does
     not hold and which CC BY-SA 3.0 share-alike does not permit.)
    Content: ChEMBL identifiers, canonical SMILES, and measured bioactivity values.
    (The 16 pose-accuracy input.yaml files also carry a ligand SMILES, but those come
     from RCSB PDB depositions, which are CC0; see the RCSB entry below.)
    Attribution: ChEMBL database, EMBL-EBI. https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chembl/
    Cite: Zdrazil B, et al. The ChEMBL Database in 2023. Nucleic Acids Res.
    NOTE ON SHARE-ALIKE: CC BY-SA 3.0 requires that adaptations of the ChEMBL
    data be distributed under compatible terms. The files listed above are
    therefore made available under CC BY-SA 3.0, NOT under Apache-2.0. The code
