TRADEMARKS
================================================================================

AlphaFold is a trademark of Google DeepMind. This project is NOT affiliated with,
endorsed by, or connected to Google DeepMind or the AlphaFold team.

The word "only" used to appear in this paragraph -- AlphaFold was said to be referred to
"only to describe what this project does NOT do". That stopped being true when the project
began using AlphaFold DB, and the sentence was left standing. To be exact about the three
different things the name covers here:

  * AlphaFold 3 is NOT run and NOT implemented. Its weights are request-only,
    non-commercial and Linux/CUDA-bound; Boltz-2 is used instead, and the AlphaFold 3
    reference exists to document that constraint. No AF3 code path exists in this
    repository.
  * AlphaFold DB IS used, substantially: 16 deposited models are downloaded under CC BY 4.0
    (see the entry above), read by the parser, shown in the structure gallery, and compared
    against Boltz-2 in data/alphafold_db_comparison.json. That is a positive use of
    AlphaFold content, not a description of something the project avoids.
  * AlphaFold SERVER is NOT used and could not be: its terms prohibit automated use for
    protein-ligand and protein-peptide binding prediction, which is what studies #9 and #10
    do. Nothing here is submitted to it.

